;; view/glon/vid_check.glon -- INTENT-4B-1: the look of a VID checkbox or
;; radio (vid_widgets.glon) when it is focused or disabled.
;;
;;   vid/checkbox/look state enabled focused
;;
;; Checkbox: the edge is the focus-ring colour while focused, the border
;; colour otherwise (the disabled border when disabled); the box is the
;; accent when checked, the input surface when not, and the disabled text /
;; surface colours when disabled; the label uses the disabled text colour.
;; Radio (its box and edge are hidden by vid/radio): the label is the accent
;; colour while focused; the glyph and label use the disabled text colour
;; when disabled.
;; The node's enabled flag follows (disabled widgets leave the Tab order and
;; take no clicks), as vid/button/set-enabled does; its visibility is the
;; caller's (Intent re-applies its own flags after this).
;;
;; vid/checkbox/set-checked keeps its own colours (enabled, unfocused);
;; call look after it when the widget may be disabled or focused.
;; state: [ kind id box check label checked theme edge ]
;; Desktop VID loader only (after vid_tabs.glon); the 64K stack is unchanged.
[
vid/checkbox/look: func [state enabled focused] [
    theme: block-at state 6
    checked: = block-at state 5 1
    view/flags block-at state 1 1 enabled 1 1
    either = block-at state 0 vid/kind-radio [
        vid/fg-color theme block-at state 4 either enabled [ either focused [ 13 ] [ 9 ] ] [ 93 ]
        vid/fg-color theme block-at state 3 either enabled [ either checked [ 13 ] [ 29 ] ] [ 93 ]
    ] [
        vid/fg-color theme block-at state 4 either enabled [ 9 ] [ 93 ]
        vid/fill-color theme block-at state 7 either focused [ 105 ] [ either enabled [ 17 ] [ 125 ] ]
        vid/fill-color theme block-at state 2 either enabled [ either checked [ 13 ] [ 21 ] ] [ either checked [ 93 ] [ 49 ] ]
    ]
    state
]
]
